{"business_id":"Zi-F-YvyVOK0k5QD7lrLOg","name":"Muriel's Jackson Square","shared_categories":"Cajun/Creole, Restaurants","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"kdqoDMuvyNedsouc1i33vQ","name":"Araña Taqueria y Cantina","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"JhpRI9m71ybWHkAqRdL0Tg","name":"The Avenue Pub","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"_Bi9kN_eR75G1eqIl7S3pA","name":"The Bulldog","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"AU-B663F3MPO7W-goWwwXA","name":"B Mac's","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0},{"business_id":"pKykk7lnD6Tf9wSzJYRyJA","name":"Starbucks","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0}],"text":[{"business_id":"c-iKAO2GBzSKjm7y1Oljcw","review_id":"Tp4CrWnJMROxbLLdiPbFDw","date":"2019-10-08T18:42:54","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.9512050151824951,"text_excerpt":"YUM. Red Fish Grill is a treat. First off, it's on the end of Bourbon Street, so the crowds are pretty large. It is always busy in here, but the staff is kind, even while you wait. Once our group got seated, we dove right in to our appetizers. We ordered the famous BBQ Oysters and the Alligator Boudin Balls. SO. GOOD. I mean, really amazing. I see why the oysters especially are so popular. 100% recommend. Our waiter was kind, but due to how busy it was, we didn't see a whole lot of him unless we waved him over. For my entree, I ordered the Shrimp and Grits. They were delicious, though very heavy. I would still order them again, but might go for something different next time, as they have ..."},{"business_id":"c-iKAO2GBzSKjm7y1Oljcw","review_id":"NhCnD_TBlDXOxHB0UtVKLQ","date":"2019-04-30T18:52:31","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.9441787600517273,"text_excerpt":"I thought this place was fantastic!!! We put our name in on a Friday night and waited about 20 minutes. It wasn't bad because the location is great so we walked around while we waited. It's a great atmosphere that is dimly lit and fairly casual. Our waiter, Ike, was amazing. He was so friendly and super attentive & helpful with everything! They gave some french bread for the table, which was great because we were so hungry. We got a bunch of entrees and shared family-style with 4 people. The alligator gumbo was soo good. Had a tiny bit of spice to it but it was so good! The crispy catfish and crawfish etouffee was probably my favorite dish. It had soo much flavor and was just delicious! W..."},{"business_id":"c-iKAO2GBzSKjm7y1Oljcw","review_id":"5YvMNII9aILKqHZBD9xZxA","date":"2012-12-15T14:02:55","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.9437986612319946,"text_excerpt":"Red Fish Grill seems like a tourist trap along the ever-so-frequented Bourbon and yet amongst the maritime tchotchkes and sea decor, I had a great time with some great eats! The red fish croquettes were decent- how could you not like something fried? Next came my alligator gumbo with some great cuts of gator sausage. Thick, rich, flavorful. This girl was in gumbo heaven-- def a MUST ORDER! I had to have some form of vegetation for the day and got the pear arugula salad. This was my first time ordering a nola salad and from then on, the trend has always been to expect the plate to be DRENCHED in vinaigrette/dressing. Overall, we all had a lovely dinner. Worth stopping in if you're looking ..."}],"visual":[{"business_id":"c-iKAO2GBzSKjm7y1Oljcw","photo_id":"nWqDDVOVYQ8IlrTlkwptbA","label":"inside","image_url":"/photos/nWqDDVOVYQ8IlrTlkwptbA.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.8861138224601746},{"business_id":"c-iKAO2GBzSKjm7y1Oljcw","photo_id":"YW4KbbtjYih90WH1A7582A","label":"drink","image_url":"/photos/YW4KbbtjYih90WH1A7582A.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.8792663812637329},{"business_id":"c-iKAO2GBzSKjm7y1Oljcw","photo_id":"cR9kUf6jI--3DjqnBvJxyA","label":"inside","image_url":"/photos/cR9kUf6jI--3DjqnBvJxyA.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.8736188411712646},{"business_id":"c-iKAO2GB